### REQ-001: AWS Secrets Manager for All Kafka Credentials

**Requirement Statement:**
All Kafka-related credentials, including Kafka Connect connector database passwords, API keys, mTLS certificate private keys, Schema Registry credentials, and external system integration credentials MUST be stored in AWS Secrets Manager. Secrets MUST use Customer Managed Keys (CMKs) for encryption at rest. Secrets MUST follow naming convention `/msk/<cluster-name>/<component>/<service-name>/<secret-type>` for centralized discovery and management.

**Rationale:**
AWS Secrets Manager provides centralized secrets storage with encryption, automatic rotation, versioning, and CloudTrail audit logging. HIPAA §164.312(a)(2)(iv) requires encryption of ePHI credentials. SOC 2 CC6.1 requires centralized credential management with access controls.

**Verification Method:**
- Automated secrets inventory scan via Python script
- Terraform validation blocking deployments with hard-coded credentials
- Quarterly secrets audit report
- CloudTrail review for secrets access patterns

**Secrets Naming Convention:**

```
/msk/<cluster-name>/<component>/<service-name>/<secret-type>

Examples:
/msk/msk-prod-cluster/kafka-connect/claims-postgres-source/database-credentials
/msk/msk-prod-cluster/kafka-connect/salesforce-sink/api-key
/msk/msk-prod-cluster/certificates/claims-adjudication-service/private-key
/msk/msk-prod-cluster/schema-registry/admin/credentials
/msk/msk-prod-cluster/lenses-io/service-account/api-token
/msk/msk-prod-cluster/mirrormaker2/replication/source-credentials
```

**Secret Structure (JSON):**

```json
{
  "username": "kafka_connect_claims_user",
  "password": "A8f$mK9#pL2@vN7*qR4",
  "host": "claims-db.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com",
  "port": 5432,
  "database": "claims_prod",
  "ssl_mode": "require",
  "created_at": "2026-02-10T10:30:00Z",
  "rotation_interval_days": 60,
  "service_owner": "claims-processing-team",
  "jira_ticket": "KAFKA-1234"
}
```

**Terraform Secret Creation:**

```hcl
# modules/kafka-secrets/main.tf

# KMS key for secrets encryption
resource "aws_kms_key" "kafka_secrets" {
  description             = "KMS key for MSK secrets encryption"
  deletion_window_in_days = 30
  enable_key_rotation     = true

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Sid    = "Enable IAM User Permissions"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          AWS = "arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:root"
        }
        Action   = "kms:*"
        Resource = "*"
      },
      {
        Sid    = "Allow Secrets Manager"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "secretsmanager.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = [
          "kms:Decrypt",
          "kms:GenerateDataKey",
          "kms:CreateGrant"
        ]
        Resource = "*"
      },
      {
        Sid    = "Allow Kafka Connect Service Role"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          AWS = aws_iam_role.kafka_connect.arn
        }
        Action = [
          "kms:Decrypt"
        ]
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })

  tags = {
    Name        = "kafka-secrets-cmk"
    Environment = var.environment
    ManagedBy   = "Terraform"
  }
}

resource "aws_kms_alias" "kafka_secrets" {
  name          = "alias/kafka-secrets-${var.environment}"
  target_key_id = aws_kms_key.kafka_secrets.key_id
}

# Secret for Kafka Connect PostgreSQL source connector
resource "aws_secretsmanager_secret" "kafka_connect_postgres" {
  for_each = var.postgres_source_connectors

  name        = "/msk/${var.cluster_name}/kafka-connect/${each.key}/database-credentials"
  description = "PostgreSQL database credentials for Kafka Connect source connector: ${each.key}"
  kms_key_id  = aws_kms_key.kafka_secrets.arn

  rotation_rules {
    automatically_after_days = each.value.rotation_interval_days  # 30, 60, or 90 days
  }

  tags = {
    Cluster     = var.cluster_name
    Connector   = each.key
    Environment = var.environment
    Owner       = each.value.service_owner
    ManagedBy   = "Terraform"
  }
}

resource "aws_secretsmanager_secret_version" "kafka_connect_postgres" {
  for_each = var.postgres_source_connectors

  secret_id = aws_secretsmanager_secret.kafka_connect_postgres[each.key].id
  secret_string = jsonencode({
    username               = each.value.username
    password               = random_password.postgres[each.key].result
    host                   = each.value.host
    port                   = each.value.port
    database               = each.value.database
    ssl_mode               = "require"
    created_at             = timestamp()
    rotation_interval_days = each.value.rotation_interval_days
    service_owner          = each.value.service_owner
    jira_ticket            = each.value.jira_ticket
  })
}

# Generate secure random passwords (32 characters with special chars)
resource "random_password" "postgres" {
  for_each = var.postgres_source_connectors

  length  = 32
  special = true
  override_special = "!@#$%^&*()-_=+[]{}|;:,.<>?"
}

# IAM policy for Kafka Connect to read secrets
resource "aws_iam_policy" "kafka_connect_secrets_access" {
  name        = "kafka-connect-secrets-access-${var.cluster_name}"
  path        = "/kafka-connect/"
  description = "Allow Kafka Connect to read secrets from Secrets Manager"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Sid    = "ReadKafkaConnectSecrets"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = [
          "secretsmanager:GetSecretValue",
          "secretsmanager:DescribeSecret"
        ]
        Resource = "arn:aws:secretsmanager:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:secret:/msk/${var.cluster_name}/kafka-connect/*"
      },
      {
        Sid    = "DecryptSecrets"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = [
          "kms:Decrypt"
        ]
        Resource = aws_kms_key.kafka_secrets.arn
        Condition = {
          StringEquals = {
            "kms:ViaService" = "secretsmanager.${var.region}.amazonaws.com"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "kafka_connect_secrets" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.kafka_connect.name
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.kafka_connect_secrets_access.arn
}
```

**Kafka Connect Connector Configuration (Using Secrets Manager):**

```json
{
  "name": "claims-postgres-source-v1",
  "config": {
    "connector.class": "io.debezium.connector.postgresql.PostgresConnector",
    "plugin.name": "pgoutput",
    "database.hostname": "${secretsManager:/msk/msk-prod-cluster/kafka-connect/claims-postgres-source/database-credentials:host}",
    "database.port": "${secretsManager:/msk/msk-prod-cluster/kafka-connect/claims-postgres-source/database-credentials:port}",
    "database.user": "${secretsManager:/msk/msk-prod-cluster/kafka-connect/claims-postgres-source/database-credentials:username}",
    "database.password": "${secretsManager:/msk/msk-prod-cluster/kafka-connect/claims-postgres-source/database-credentials:password}",
    "database.dbname": "${secretsManager:/msk/msk-prod-cluster/kafka-connect/claims-postgres-source/database-credentials:database}",
    "database.server.name": "claims-db",
    "table.include.list": "public.claims,public.members,public.providers",
    "topic.prefix": "claims.postgres",
    "slot.name": "kafka_connect_claims_slot",
    "publication.name": "kafka_connect_claims_pub",
    "tasks.max": "3"
  }
}
```

